WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.470
The Avengers launched the careers of some
of Hollywood's biggest stars.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.620
But just how did these celebs prepare themselves
for life?

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.839
Did they spend hours and hours studying, or
did they toss away their books and try to

00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:14.440
gain some real-world experience instead?

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.260
Here’s how far the Avengers all got in school.

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:23.980
According to late Marvel legend Stan Lee,
Robert Downey Jr. was "born to be" Tony Stark.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.800
Growing up at the center of the avant-garde
scene of the '70s with a writer-actress mother

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.329
and filmmaker father, he made his on-screen
debut at the age of five in Robert Downey

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:35.820
Sr.'s movie Pound.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.460
Downey Jr. told Vanity Fair in 2014 that his
parents moved around a lot for work during

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.010
this time, meaning he had to learn the craft
along the way.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.899
While receiving a basic education in various
cities, Downey also studied classical ballet

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:55.859
at the Perry House in London and trained in
acting at New York’s Stagedoor Manor Performing

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:57.469
Arts Training Center.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:02.140
According to CNN, he dropped out of Santa
Monica High School and attempted to to focus

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:03.440
on his acting career.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.450
“I don’t know if I ever really had that
thought that this is what I was going to do.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.100
It never occurred to me to do anything else.”

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.400
Chris Evans always knew he wanted to be an
actor.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:17.010
According to The New York Times, he spent
his youth performing in school plays in his

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.920
Massachusetts hometown, where he was voted
"Most Theatrical."

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:26.130
After graduating high school in the late '90s,
the aspiring actor moved directly to New York

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.500
City to pursue his professional career.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.840
In 2017, Evans told The Los Angeles Times:

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:38.240
"To be honest, it could be a cocktail of naiveté
mixed with confidence but certainly at the

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.090
time I didn't have much doubt.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:45.230
A lot of that I attribute it to the people
around me, my parents, who said go for it.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.140
Go to New York.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.360
You can do it."

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:52.240
Evans may have opted out of attending college,
but he did go on to train in method acting

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.680
at the Lee Strasberg Theatre and Film Institute.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.860
Mark Ruffalo may have gained international
recognition for his portrayal of Bruce Banner,

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:05.700
but he got his start as a wrestler with a
secret passion for acting at his school in

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:11.780
Virginia Beach where he also struggled with
undiagnosed dyslexia, ADHD, and depression.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:16.500
Tempted by the possibility of receiving a
full-ride scholarship, he quit the wrestling

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.600
team and tried his hand at acting during his
senior year.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.280
With his parents' support, the aspiring actor
skipped the college applications and quietly

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.470
pursued his career in San Diego, but later
admitted to New York Magazine:

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.909
"I lied to all my friends and told them I
was going to UCSD … 'cause I felt it was

00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:36.100
unrealistic to be an actor."

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.129
Ruffalo went on hundreds of failed auditions
during his 20s while making a living as a

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:45.320
bartender which may have helped him later
tap into the Hulk's rage.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.659
In 2015, he told Rolling Stone:

00:02:47.659 --> 00:02:52.400
"The frustration I was having with acting
made me angry all the time."

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.939
While studying acting at the Stella Adler
Conservatory in Los Angeles, Ruffalo also

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:03.060
co-founded the Orpheus Theatre Company, where
he wrote, directed, and acted in several productions.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.560
According to the Film Festival Traveler, Chris
Hemsworth grew up in Melbourne and received

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:13.650
his secondary education at Heathmont College,
before launching his career on the soap opera

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:14.650
circuit.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.129
He trained in acting and reportedly mastered
his American accent at the Screenwise Film

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:21.340
&amp; TV school for Actors in Sydney.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.720
“You have no idea what you’re dealing
with.”

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:25.140
“Ah…

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.020
Shakespeare in the park?”

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.700
Ahead of filming on the first Thor movie,
Hemsworth was aware that he was one of the

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:37.319
only cast members who didn't have a prestigious
educational background but never viewed this

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.660
as a disadvantage.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.700
He told Film Festival Traveller:

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.100
"People like that elevate your game, and if
you leave yourself open to learn from them

00:03:45.109 --> 00:03:48.689
and walk in with humility, I guess then it
becomes back-and-forth.

00:03:48.689 --> 00:03:54.189
[...] Just work hard and be open to exploring
different ideas and taking risks and going

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:56.200
with the spontaneity of it all."

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.200
Scarlett Johansson

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:01.931
Scarlett Johansson already had several movies
under her belt by the time she was 19, when

00:04:01.931 --> 00:04:06.560
she decided to ditch her plans to study film
at SUNY Purchase.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.040
In 2004, she told New York Magazine:

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.620
"I don't miss school.

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:12.799
It's for some people and not for others."

00:04:12.799 --> 00:04:17.850
Johansson began her career as a child, while
attending P.S. 41 elementary school in New

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:18.620
York City.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:23.400
Amid commercial auditions, dance lessons,
and sporadic work in theater and film, she

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:28.570
went on to study acting at the prestigious
Lee Strasberg Theatre Institute for Kids and

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.630
the Professional Children's School.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.150
In 2005, she told The Independent:

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.490
"Acting has been a passion of mine.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.540
My childhood was filled with things that I
loved to do, and also very normal things:

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:43.740
I lived in New York, I have a family life
and went to a regular school."

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:49.600
Jeremy Renner already had about three dozen
credits — and two Oscar nominations — before

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.860
landing the role of archer Clint Barton in
the MCU.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:58.560
However, this bona fide movie star's initial
venture into acting was a total fluke.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:04.060
While studying computer science and criminology
at Modesto Junior College in the early '90s,

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:07.700
he took a drama course and immediately caught
the acting bug.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.290
“What, you didn’t see that coming?”

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:15.890
The actor's former professor, Charline Freedman,
called him one of her best students ever,

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.160
telling The Modesto Bee:

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:22.290
"I would say within a month, I knew we had
somebody very special in this young man."

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:27.780
For his part, Renner has often credited his
time at MJC for helping him launch his successful

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:28.280
career.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.640
Referring to Freedman as "my gal," he said:

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.880
"[She] pointed me in the direction that I
never turned back from."

